% Test cases for the respiratory assist device policy (rad.le): synthetic
% claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33800, each stating only what its
% record shows. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's or the
% Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer conditional. The
% queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query, so "stage" reads
% its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and what minimal
% change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base rad cases includes these resources:
    rad.

the knowledge base rad cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim for an E0471 for a restrictive thoracic
% disorder (ALS, a neuromuscular disease; criterion B by the awake PaCO2):
% every criterion and every documentation requirement in the record.
scenario rtd_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0471".
    the RAD device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ann documents neuromuscular disease.
    the medical record of Ann documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Ann done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 48 mm Hg.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the RAD device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the RAD device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the RAD device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the RAD device includes order date.
    the order for the RAD device includes description of the item.
    the order for the RAD device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the RAD device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the RAD device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the RAD device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the RAD device.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A severe thoracic cage abnormality qualifying by sleep oximetry (86 percent
% for 12 minutes of a 6-hour recording): criterion B2, an E0470.
scenario rtd_oximetry is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0470".
    the RAD device is furnished to Ben.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 2.
    the medical record of Ben documents severe thoracic cage abnormality.
    the medical record of Ben documents morning headache.
    the sleep oximetry of Ben on the prescribed FIO2 shows oxygen saturation at or below 86 percent for 12 minutes.
    the recording time of the sleep oximetry of Ben is 6 hours.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Criterion B3 (a forced vital capacity of 42 percent of predicted) is for a
% neuromuscular disease only: it qualifies Cy (neuromuscular disease), not
% Dee (thoracic cage abnormality).
scenario rtd_fvc_neuromuscular_only is:
    claim 1 is for the first device.
    the HCPCS code of the first device is "E0470".
    the first device is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Cy documents neuromuscular disease.
    the medical record of Cy documents dyspnea.
    the forced vital capacity of Cy is 42 percent of predicted.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 2 is for the second device.
    the HCPCS code of the second device is "E0470".
    the second device is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the medical record of Dee documents severe thoracic cage abnormality.
    the medical record of Dee documents dyspnea.
    the forced vital capacity of Dee is 42 percent of predicted.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% An awake PaCO2 of 43 mm Hg, a maximal inspiratory pressure of 65 cm H2O:
% no alternative of criterion B is met.
scenario rtd_tests_below_threshold is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0470".
    the RAD device is furnished to Eve.
    the residence of Eve is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Eve documents neuromuscular disease.
    the medical record of Eve documents excessive fatigue.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Eve done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 43 mm Hg.
    the maximal inspiratory pressure of Eve is 65 cm H2O.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% No symptom of sleep-associated hypoventilation documented: not covered for
% any disorder.
scenario rtd_no_symptoms is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0471".
    the RAD device is furnished to Fay.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Fay documents neuromuscular disease.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Fay done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 52 mm Hg.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% Nothing says whether COPD contributes to the limitation: the answer is
% conditional on that finding. When the Council finds the record shows a
% significant COPD contribution, the claim is not reasonable and necessary.
scenario rtd_copd_contribution_open is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0470".
    the RAD device is furnished to Gus.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Gus documents neuromuscular disease.
    the medical record of Gus documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Gus done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 49 mm Hg.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding copd contribution insignificant about Gus is established"].

scenario rtd_copd_contribution_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0470".
    the RAD device is furnished to Gus.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Gus documents neuromuscular disease.
    the medical record of Gus documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Gus done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 49 mm Hg.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Gus is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the pulmonary function tests show severe airflow obstruction and the record attributes the hypercapnia to COPD".
    rn expects answers [].

% Central sleep apnea: a facility-based attended polysomnogram before
% delivery (AHI 22, 70 percent central events, CAHI 14, sleepiness, no
% hypoventilation documented) and the practitioner's finding that the
% hypoventilation improved on the device.
scenario csa_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0471".
    the RAD device is furnished to Hal.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Hal documents excessive fatigue.
    the medical record of Hal documents sleepiness.
    the sleep test of Hal was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Hal is facility polysomnogram.
    the sleep test of Hal was attended.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Hal is 22.
    central apneas and central hypopneas are 70 percent of the apneas and hypopneas of the sleep test of Hal.
    the CAHI of the sleep test of Hal is 14.
    the finding hypoventilation improved on device about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the RAD device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The same record with a home sleep test, and with the central events at 40
% percent of the total: neither is central sleep apnea under the LCD.
scenario csa_not_established is:
    claim 1 is for the first device.
    the HCPCS code of the first device is "E0471".
    the first device is furnished to Ida.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ida documents excessive fatigue.
    the medical record of Ida documents sleepiness.
    the sleep test of Ida was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ida is home sleep test.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ida is 22.
    central apneas and central hypopneas are 70 percent of the apneas and hypopneas of the sleep test of Ida.
    the CAHI of the sleep test of Ida is 14.
    the finding hypoventilation improved on device about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the first device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    claim 2 is for the second device.
    the HCPCS code of the second device is "E0471".
    the second device is furnished to Jo.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the medical record of Jo documents excessive fatigue.
    the medical record of Jo documents sleepiness.
    the sleep test of Jo was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Jo is facility polysomnogram.
    the sleep test of Jo was attended.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Jo is 22.
    central apneas and central hypopneas are 40 percent of the apneas and hypopneas of the sleep test of Jo.
    the CAHI of the sleep test of Jo is 14.
    the finding hypoventilation improved on device about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the second device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    rn expects answers [].

% Complex sleep apnea: on titration with a device without backup rate the
% obstructive AHI fell to 3 while central events persisted (65 percent, CAHI
% 9).
scenario compsa_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0470".
    the RAD device is furnished to Kim.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Kim documents cognitive dysfunction.
    the sleep test of Kim was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Kim is facility polysomnogram.
    the sleep test of Kim was attended.
    the titration of Kim on a PAP device without backup rate reached an obstructive AHI of 3.
    after resolution of the obstructive events central apneas and central hypopneas are 65 percent of the apneas and hypopneas of Kim.
    after resolution of the obstructive events the CAHI of Kim is 9.
    the finding hypoventilation improved on device about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the RAD device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Hypoventilation syndrome, E0470: initial awake PaCO2 47, FEV1/FVC 76,
% PaCO2 during sleep 55 (criterion C). Lee, with the same record but an
% FEV1/FVC of 62, fails criterion B (that is the COPD route).
scenario hs_e0470_sleep_abg is:
    claim 1 is for the first device.
    the HCPCS code of the first device is "E0470".
    the first device is furnished to Liv.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Liv documents hypoventilation syndrome.
    the medical record of Liv documents morning headache.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Liv done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 47 mm Hg.
    the FEV1 to FVC ratio of the spirometry of Liv is 76 percent.
    the PaCO2 of the arterial blood gas of Liv done during sleep or immediately upon awakening on the prescribed FIO2 is 55 mm Hg.
    claim 2 is for the second device.
    the HCPCS code of the second device is "E0470".
    the second device is furnished to Lee.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the medical record of Lee documents hypoventilation syndrome.
    the medical record of Lee documents morning headache.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Lee done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 47 mm Hg.
    the FEV1 to FVC ratio of the spirometry of Lee is 62 percent.
    the PaCO2 of the arterial blood gas of Lee done during sleep or immediately upon awakening on the prescribed FIO2 is 55 mm Hg.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Hypoventilation syndrome by criterion D: a home sleep test with saturation
% at or below 87 percent for 8 minutes of a 5-hour recording and an AHI of 2
% qualifies Max; Ned's desaturation comes with an AHI of 18 (obstructive)
% and does not.
scenario hs_e0470_desaturation is:
    claim 1 is for the first device.
    the HCPCS code of the first device is "E0470".
    the first device is furnished to Max.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Max documents hypoventilation syndrome.
    the medical record of Max documents dyspnea.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Max done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 46 mm Hg.
    the FEV1 to FVC ratio of the spirometry of Max is 80 percent.
    the type of the sleep test of Max is home sleep test.
    the sleep test of Max shows oxygen saturation at or below 87 percent for 8 minutes.
    the recording time of the sleep test of Max is 5 hours.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Max is 2.
    claim 2 is for the second device.
    the HCPCS code of the second device is "E0470".
    the second device is furnished to Ned.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the medical record of Ned documents hypoventilation syndrome.
    the medical record of Ned documents dyspnea.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Ned done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 46 mm Hg.
    the FEV1 to FVC ratio of the spirometry of Ned is 80 percent.
    the type of the sleep test of Ned is home sleep test.
    the sleep test of Ned shows oxygen saturation at or below 87 percent for 8 minutes.
    the recording time of the sleep test of Ned is 5 hours.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ned is 18.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% An E0471 for hypoventilation syndrome: a covered E0470 in use, and the
% awake PaCO2 on it worsened by 9 mm Hg (56 against 47). Without the
% follow-up blood gas (Pam) the E0471 is not covered, though an E0470 is.
scenario hs_e0471 is:
    claim 1 is for the first device.
    the HCPCS code of the first device is "E0471".
    the first device is furnished to Oli.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Oli documents hypoventilation syndrome.
    the medical record of Oli documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Oli done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 47 mm Hg.
    the FEV1 to FVC ratio of the spirometry of Oli is 74 percent.
    the PaCO2 of the arterial blood gas of Oli done during sleep or immediately upon awakening on the prescribed FIO2 is 58 mm Hg.
    Oli is using an E0470 device.
    the PaCO2 of the follow-up arterial blood gas of Oli done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 during use of the E0470 device is 56 mm Hg.
    claim 2 is for the second device.
    the HCPCS code of the second device is "E0471".
    the second device is furnished to Pam.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the medical record of Pam documents hypoventilation syndrome.
    the medical record of Pam documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Pam done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 47 mm Hg.
    the FEV1 to FVC ratio of the spirometry of Pam is 74 percent.
    the PaCO2 of the arterial blood gas of Pam done during sleep or immediately upon awakening on the prescribed FIO2 is 58 mm Hg.
    Pam is using an E0470 device.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% An E0470 for obstructive sleep apnea: a PAP claim (pap.le), not a RAD
% claim — no rule of this policy covers it.
scenario e0470_for_osa is:
    claim 1 is for the bilevel device.
    the HCPCS code of the bilevel device is "E0470".
    the bilevel device is furnished to Ray.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ray documents obstructive sleep apnea.
    the medical record of Ray documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the type of the sleep test of Ray is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ray is 32.
    rn expects answers [].

% Chronic respiratory failure consequent to COPD: the NCD's initial criteria
% found met carry the first six months (claim 1, month 5); month 8 (claim 2)
% needs the NCD's continuing usage criteria, which nobody has found.
scenario copd is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0471".
    the RAD device is furnished to Sam.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 5.
    claim 2 is for the RAD device.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 8.
    the medical record of Sam documents chronic respiratory failure consequent to COPD.
    the medical record of Sam documents dyspnea.
    the finding copd ncd initial criteria met about Sam is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding copd ncd continuing criteria met about Sam is established"].

% Month 4 of a restrictive thoracic disorder: re-evaluated on day 70 of use,
% 5.2 hours a day, the progress documented, the practitioner's statement
% signed on day 70.
scenario month_4_compliant is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0471".
    the RAD device is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    the medical record of Ann documents neuromuscular disease.
    the medical record of Ann documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Ann done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 48 mm Hg.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the RAD device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    Ann was re-evaluated by the treating practitioner on 2026-05-10.
    the medical record of Ann documents the progress of symptoms and the usage of the RAD device.
    the average use of the RAD device by Ann by the time of the re-evaluation is 5.2 hours per day.
    the supplier holds a statement signed and dated by the treating practitioner on 2026-05-10 declaring that Ann is compliantly using and benefiting from the RAD device.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Month 4 with the re-evaluation on day 45 (Tia) and, for Uma, on day 70 but
% with 3 hours of use a day: continued coverage fails.
scenario month_4_not_continued is:
    claim 1 is for the first device.
    the HCPCS code of the first device is "E0471".
    the first device is furnished to Tia.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    the medical record of Tia documents neuromuscular disease.
    the medical record of Tia documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Tia done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 48 mm Hg.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Tia is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the first device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    Tia was re-evaluated by the treating practitioner on 2026-04-15.
    the medical record of Tia documents the progress of symptoms and the usage of the first device.
    the average use of the first device by Tia by the time of the re-evaluation is 6 hours per day.
    the supplier holds a statement signed and dated by the treating practitioner on 2026-04-15 declaring that Tia is compliantly using and benefiting from the first device.
    claim 2 is for the second device.
    the HCPCS code of the second device is "E0471".
    the second device is furnished to Uma.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-06-01.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 4.
    the medical record of Uma documents neuromuscular disease.
    the medical record of Uma documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Uma done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 48 mm Hg.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Uma is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the second device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    Uma was re-evaluated by the treating practitioner on 2026-05-10.
    the medical record of Uma documents the progress of symptoms and the usage of the second device.
    the average use of the second device by Uma by the time of the re-evaluation is 3 hours per day.
    the supplier holds a statement signed and dated by the treating practitioner on 2026-05-10 declaring that Uma is compliantly using and benefiting from the second device.
    rn expects answers [].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the RAD device.
    the HCPCS code of the RAD device is "E0471".
    the RAD device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ann documents neuromuscular disease.
    the medical record of Ann documents daytime hypersomnolence.
    the PaCO2 of the initial arterial blood gas of Ann done while awake on the prescribed FIO2 is 48 mm Hg.
    the finding copd contribution insignificant about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the RAD device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the RAD device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the RAD device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the RAD device includes order date.
    the order for the RAD device includes description of the item.
    the order for the RAD device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the RAD device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the RAD device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the RAD device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the RAD device"]].
